    "caveats": [
      "Monetary fields are stored directly as currency amounts; no cents-to-dollars conversion is required. Currency code is explicitly USD only for part retail price, while other monetary fields are described generically as currency amounts.",
      "`orders.o_totalprice` is an order-level total. Do not sum it after joining to `lineitem`, because each order is repeated once per line item; aggregate orders first or use `SUM(DISTINCT o_totalprice)` only if each distinct value safely represents one order (generally prefer pre-aggregation).",
      "Line-item revenue metrics are derived from `l_extendedprice`, `l_discount` (a 0\u20131 fraction), and `l_tax` (a 0\u20131 fraction). `l_extendedprice` is pre-discount; net revenue excludes tax unless using the tax-inclusive metric.",
      "To connect a line item to a specific supplier offering/cost record, join `lineitem` to `partsupp` on both part and supplier keys: `l_partkey = ps_partkey AND l_suppkey = ps_suppkey`. Joining on only one key can cause fan-out and incorrect totals.",
      "`partsupp` is at part-supplier grain, so inventory and supply-cost analyses should be aggregated from that table and not joined indiscriminately to line items or parts.",
      "Joining customer or supplier to nation and region is many-to-one and safe for grouping. Joining orders to customer and line items to orders expands parent rows to child grain; calculate parent-grain metrics before such joins.",
      "`l_shipdate`, `l_commitdate`, and `l_receiptdate` cover different operational events. Use `o_orderdate` for order-placement trends and the appropriate line-item date for fulfillment or shipping trends.",
      "Order dates range from 1992-01-01 to 1998-08-02; line-item shipment, commitment, and receipt dates extend into late 1998. Date-based comparisons should account for these different coverage windows.",
      "`o_shippriority` has only the observed value 0, so it is not useful for segmentation in this dataset.",
      "Customer and supplier account balances may be negative and are account-balance attributes, not sales, revenue, or payable amounts."
    ],
    "example_questions": [
